WEBVTT

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:00.776
you're often more focused
on your own needs.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:04.016
But gratitude makes you
want to pay it forward.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:06.456
And I experienced this personally.

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:08.176
I mean, I'm not Mother Teresa,

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:11.656
I'm still a selfish bastard
a huge amount of the time.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:15.656
But I'm better than I was
before this project.

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:18.416
And that's because it made me aware

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:22.016
of the exploitation on the supply chain.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.976
It reminded me
that what I take for granted

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:28.776
is not available to millions
of people around the world.

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:30.056
Like water.